Below is a list of all schematic symbols that would be required to build a 36 V bus‑monitoring circuit around the INA226 device.  
The list includes the INA226 itself, a shunt resistor, a simple voltage‑divider network, a generic small resistor for pull‑ups, and the necessary power supply symbols. All symbols are taken from the libraries that were supplied in the prompt.

| Symbol | Library |
|--------|---------|
| INA226 | Sensor_Energy |
| R_Shunt | Device |
| VoltageDivider | Device |
| R_Small | Device |
| +36V | power |
| GND | power |

These symbols cover the core functionality: the INA226 measures bus voltage and shunt current; the shunt resistor provides the sense element; the voltage divider scales the 36 V bus down to the INA226’s input range; the small resistor can be used for I²C pull‑ups; and the power symbols supply the bus voltage and ground reference.

